# The launcher (domains/teleoperation/launcher): the window that starts the sim, the station, the
# radio wizard and the manual build. Its driver (`sim001_launcher --expect`, src/expect.rs) clicks
# the real buttons of the real window and reads back what the launcher started. In the tests the
# launcher starts a stand-in of itself in place of each program (`--stand-in`): the stand-in
# waits until it is stopped, so the log, the job and STOP are real,
# but nothing flies. The controls.cfg of a test is in a data folder of the test's own.

Section: The launcher
  On: desktop
  The launcher is the window that you start SIM001 from. It starts the sim alone, or the whole
  ground station, or a game of Towers. It also sets up your controllers and opens this manual. In the app bundle,
  open `SIM001.app`. From source, type `cargo run --release` in the top folder of the repository.

  The window has four screens. LAUNCH starts the sim or the station. CONTROLLERS lists the
  radios and gamepads that are plugged in, and what `controls.cfg` maps. DOCS opens this
  manual. LOG shows the output of the program that runs. The launcher runs one program at a
  time. Press STOP, or close the launcher, to end that program and all that it started.

  A radio with USB Serial (VCP) set to LUA shows up as a serial device, not as a joystick.
  The launcher finds it and lists it under CONTROLLERS. With ArduPilot, TX15 ON SERIAL starts
  the station on that device. The sticks, the telemetry and the MAVLink of the console then go
  through the radio, as on the real plane. See [[The flight computer]].

  Start with [[Your first flight from the launcher]]. Then set up your controls with
  [[Setting up your radio]].

Vocabulary:
  # The choices on the LAUNCH screen: the lit button of each pair.
  State: the launch target is SIMULATOR ONLY | GROUND STATION | TOWERS
    Set: click {value}
    Shows: the {value} button is lit green
  State: the Red team is COMPUTER | NOBODY
    Set: click RED: {value}
    Shows: the RED: {value} button is lit green
  State: the drone cameras choice is on | off
    Set: click DRONE CAMERAS until it is {value}
    Shows: on: the DRONE CAMERAS button is lit green
  State: the flight controller choice is WITH ARDUPILOT | WITHOUT ARDUPILOT
    Set: click {value}
    Shows: the {value} button is lit green
  State: the place choice is ALPINE VALLEY | CYPRESS | BERKELEY
    Set: click {value} under Place
    Shows: the {value} button is lit green
  State: the ray tracing choice is on | off
    Set: click RAY TRACING until it is {value}
    Shows: on: the RAY TRACING button is lit green
  State: the launch button is LAUNCH | STOP
    Shows: LAUNCH: the green button at the bottom of the LAUNCH screen reads LAUNCH
    Shows: STOP: the button at the bottom of the LAUNCH screen is red and reads STOP

  # The program that the launcher started, as the LOG screen shows it: its name, its state,
  # and its command line in the first line of the log.
  State: the program in the log is nothing | the simulator | the ground station | the Towers game | the radio wizard | the manual build
    Shows: nothing: the LOG screen says "Nothing running"
    Shows: the simulator: the name of the program on the LOG screen starts with "Simulator"
    Shows: the ground station: the name of the program on the LOG screen starts with "Ground station"
    Shows: the Towers game: the name of the program on the LOG screen starts with "Towers"
    Shows: the radio wizard: the LOG screen says "Controller setup"
    Shows: the manual build: the LOG screen says "Render the docs"
  State: the program is idle | running | stopped
    Shows: idle: no program runs
    Shows: running: the LOG screen says running, in green, beside the name of the program
    Shows: stopped: the LOG screen says ended, in red, beside the name of the program
  State: the plane of the started sim is none | the T1-S VTOL | the T1-S Ranger
    Shows: the T1-S VTOL: the command in the first line of the log has `--aircraft t1s-vtol`
    Shows: the T1-S Ranger: the command in the first line of the log has `--aircraft t1s-ranger`
  State: the sticks of the started station are through ArduPilot | direct
    Shows: through ArduPilot: the command in the first line of the log has `--station`, and not `--direct`
    Shows: direct: the command in the first line of the log has `--station --direct`
  State: the Red team of the started game is the computer | nobody
    Shows: the computer: the command in the first line of the log has `--serve`, and not `--red nobody`
    Shows: nobody: the command in the first line of the log has `--serve --red nobody`
  State: the drone cameras of the started game are on | off
    Shows: on: the command in the first line of the log has `--serve`, and not `--no-cameras`
    Shows: off: the command in the first line of the log has `--no-cameras`
  State: the place of the started program is the Alpine Valley | Cypress | Berkeley
    Shows: the Alpine Valley: the command in the first line of the log has no `--map`
    Shows: Cypress: the command in the first line of the log has `--map cypress`
    Shows: Berkeley: the command in the first line of the log has `--map berkeley`
  State: the ray tracing of the started program is on | off
    Shows: on: the command in the first line of the log has `--raytrace`
    Shows: off: the command in the first line of the log has no `--raytrace`

  # What the CONTROLLERS screen says about controls.cfg.
  State: the controls file is missing | mapped
    Set: missing: if you have a `controls.cfg`, delete it. It is in `~/Library/Application Support/SIM001` on macOS
    Shows: missing: the CONTROLLERS screen says "No controls.cfg yet"
    Shows: mapped: the CONTROLLERS screen says "controls.cfg maps" and the number of channels

  Event: the pilot launches
    Say: click LAUNCH
  Event: the pilot stops the program
    Say: click STOP
  Event: the pilot sets up the controller
    Say: click SET UP CONTROLLER. The sim opens on the plain T1-S, with the radio wizard
  Event: the radio wizard saves controls.cfg and closes
    Say: move each stick and switch when the wizard asks. The wizard saves `controls.cfg`. Then close the sim
  Event: the pilot renders the docs
    Say: click RENDER DOCS

  Phrase: the launcher has just opened
    Say: start the launcher. In the app bundle, open `SIM001.app`. From source, type `cargo run --release` in the top folder of the repository
    Given the launch target is GROUND STATION
    And the flight controller choice is WITH ARDUPILOT
    And the place choice is ALPINE VALLEY
    And the ray tracing choice is off
    And the program in the log is nothing
    And the program is idle
    And the launch button is LAUNCH

Background:
  Given the launcher has just opened
